1
00:00:00,862 --> 00:00:03,219
This episode reads exactly one paper:

2
00:00:03,324 --> 00:00:05,582
the FlyCircuit paper from twenty eleven.

3
00:00:06,324 --> 00:00:08,569
It is about one thing that paper proposed

4
00:00:08,624 --> 00:00:11,169
— the L P U, the local processing unit.

5
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,812
What it does is turn "brain region" from

6
00:00:13,812 --> 00:00:16,074
an anatomical noun into a definition that

7
00:00:16,074 --> 00:00:17,987
can be run automatically, and that

8
00:00:17,987 --> 00:00:19,144
can be overturned.

9
00:00:20,513 --> 00:00:22,358
Why does this deserve a whole episode?

10
00:00:23,101 --> 00:00:25,313
Because later papers open with "forty nine

11
00:00:25,313 --> 00:00:27,801
nodes" and "L P U level modules", and

12
00:00:27,801 --> 00:00:29,933
hardly anyone goes back and asks:

13
00:00:30,038 --> 00:00:31,976
how were those units arrived at, and would

14
00:00:31,976 --> 00:00:33,796
a different criterion change them?

15
00:00:34,538 --> 00:00:36,251
That is exactly what you should check

16
00:00:36,251 --> 00:00:38,263
first in any paper that uses "brain

17
00:00:38,263 --> 00:00:40,463
region" as its unit, because how you cut

18
00:00:40,463 --> 00:00:42,276
the brain up determines what structure you

19
00:00:42,276 --> 00:00:44,921
can see. Seven lessons:

20
00:00:44,963 --> 00:00:47,176
the problem, two kinds of neuron, the

21
00:00:47,176 --> 00:00:49,858
definition, how it runs, what came out,

22
00:00:49,988 --> 00:00:52,088
what you can do once you have units, and

23
00:00:52,088 --> 00:00:53,771
where the definition is loose.

24
00:00:55,141 --> 00:00:58,091
Lesson one. Who decides where a brain

25
00:00:58,091 --> 00:01:01,416
region ends. Traditionally, brain regions

26
00:01:01,416 --> 00:01:03,128
are marked out by the boundaries you can

27
00:01:03,128 --> 00:01:04,511
see in a stained sample.

28
00:01:05,253 --> 00:01:07,228
The fly brain has some fifty odd of these

29
00:01:07,228 --> 00:01:09,798
blocks of dense fiber, called neuropils.

30
00:01:10,541 --> 00:01:12,553
The standard brain in this paper resolves

31
00:01:12,553 --> 00:01:15,216
fifty eight of them. The trouble is that a

32
00:01:15,216 --> 00:01:17,366
boundary you can see does not necessarily

33
00:01:17,366 --> 00:01:19,261
correspond to a functional unit.

34
00:01:20,003 --> 00:01:21,853
Two neighbouring blocks may be two halves

35
00:01:21,853 --> 00:01:25,041
of one circuit. One large block may hide

36
00:01:25,041 --> 00:01:27,398
several small units working independently.

37
00:01:28,141 --> 00:01:30,003
If what you want to know is how signals

38
00:01:30,003 --> 00:01:31,903
flow through the brain, then cutting it up

39
00:01:31,903 --> 00:01:33,891
by shape means you used a criterion

40
00:01:33,891 --> 00:01:35,691
unrelated to your question before the

41
00:01:35,691 --> 00:01:37,248
question was even asked.

42
00:01:37,991 --> 00:01:40,066
And every network analysis after that is

43
00:01:40,066 --> 00:01:41,436
built on the same cut.

44
00:01:42,178 --> 00:01:44,561
Cut it wrong, and the error is invisible.

45
00:01:45,944 --> 00:01:48,732
Lesson two. Before you can change

46
00:01:48,732 --> 00:01:50,744
criteria, you need something to use as

47
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:54,202
one. The paper uses a very simple split.

48
00:01:54,944 --> 00:01:57,657
An L N, a local neuron, stays entirely

49
00:01:57,657 --> 00:01:59,264
inside one brain region.

50
00:02:00,007 --> 00:02:01,364
Think of a city street.

51
00:02:02,107 --> 00:02:04,919
A P N, a projection neuron, connects two

52
00:02:04,919 --> 00:02:07,769
or more regions. Think of an interstate

53
00:02:07,769 --> 00:02:10,719
highway. This split is possible because

54
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:12,769
the earlier work had already turned every

55
00:02:12,769 --> 00:02:14,444
neuron into something you can compute

56
00:02:14,444 --> 00:02:17,519
with. Once a neuron is registered into the

57
00:02:17,519 --> 00:02:19,982
standard brain, how many voxels its fibers

58
00:02:19,982 --> 00:02:21,969
occupy in each of the fifty eight blocks

59
00:02:21,969 --> 00:02:24,119
is recorded, and compressed into a string

60
00:02:24,119 --> 00:02:27,182
of numbers. Whether a neuron is local or

61
00:02:27,182 --> 00:02:28,969
projecting is just the shape of that

62
00:02:28,969 --> 00:02:31,482
string: concentrated in one bin, or

63
00:02:31,482 --> 00:02:32,752
spread across several.

64
00:02:34,132 --> 00:02:36,314
On screen is the paper's third figure.

65
00:02:37,057 --> 00:02:39,357
Panels A to C follow one neuron as it is

66
00:02:39,357 --> 00:02:41,557
cut out of a sample brain, registered into

67
00:02:41,557 --> 00:02:43,494
the standard brain, and traced into a

68
00:02:43,494 --> 00:02:46,739
skeleton. The panel that matters is D:

69
00:02:46,857 --> 00:02:49,144
how many voxels this one neuron occupies

70
00:02:49,144 --> 00:02:51,214
in each of twenty nine paired blocks.

71
00:02:51,957 --> 00:02:54,232
From here on, every analysis happens in

72
00:02:54,232 --> 00:02:57,169
that number space. Nothing goes back to

73
00:02:57,169 --> 00:03:00,157
the original image. And the cost is right

74
00:03:00,157 --> 00:03:03,639
here too. How a fiber runs inside a block,

75
00:03:03,694 --> 00:03:05,757
where it branches, is discarded at this

76
00:03:05,757 --> 00:03:07,739
step, and it cannot be recovered.

77
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:12,427
Lesson three. The criterion itself.

78
00:03:13,170 --> 00:03:15,120
If a brain region holds a group of local

79
00:03:15,120 --> 00:03:17,295
neurons of its own, interweaving inside

80
00:03:17,295 --> 00:03:19,320
it, that means there is local processing

81
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:21,170
going on there, and it counts as an

82
00:03:21,170 --> 00:03:22,877
independent processing unit.

83
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:26,952
An L P U. The intuition is this.

84
00:03:27,695 --> 00:03:29,732
A place with only highways passing through

85
00:03:29,732 --> 00:03:32,090
and no city streets is a transfer station,

86
00:03:32,182 --> 00:03:35,157
not a city. Having a street network of its

87
00:03:35,157 --> 00:03:37,465
own means whatever arrives gets worked on,

88
00:03:37,595 --> 00:03:39,277
rather than passed straight through.

89
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:42,095
The full definition the paper writes down

90
00:03:42,095 --> 00:03:43,440
has three conditions.

91
00:03:44,182 --> 00:03:46,195
It has a local neuron population of its

92
00:03:46,195 --> 00:03:48,895
own. Those fibers are completely

93
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:50,352
restricted to that region.

94
00:03:51,095 --> 00:03:53,415
And at least one nerve tract touches it.

95
00:03:54,787 --> 00:03:56,737
Stop here, because this is the most

96
00:03:56,737 --> 00:03:58,557
important sentence in the episode.

97
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:01,282
The L P U is not a discovery.

98
00:04:02,025 --> 00:04:04,162
It is a definition, and one that can be

99
00:04:04,162 --> 00:04:05,782
overturned by its own data.

100
00:04:06,525 --> 00:04:08,400
Its value is not in how accurate the

101
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,420
number forty one turns out to be.

102
00:04:11,162 --> 00:04:13,287
It is in turning "what is a brain region"

103
00:04:13,287 --> 00:04:15,062
from a question that needs an expert's

104
00:04:15,062 --> 00:04:16,975
judgment into a question with steps you

105
00:04:16,975 --> 00:04:19,407
can write down, a result you can compute,

106
00:04:19,525 --> 00:04:20,950
and a different answer when the data

107
00:04:20,950 --> 00:04:23,887
change. The last lesson will show that

108
00:04:23,887 --> 00:04:26,082
"gives a different answer" is not a flaw.

109
00:04:26,825 --> 00:04:28,850
It is precisely what qualifies it as a

110
00:04:28,850 --> 00:04:30,345
scientific definition.

111
00:04:31,719 --> 00:04:34,694
Lesson four. How do you actually find

112
00:04:34,694 --> 00:04:36,356
these units among sixteen thousand

113
00:04:36,356 --> 00:04:39,244
neurons? The paper writes it as seven

114
00:04:39,244 --> 00:04:42,494
steps. Count how often local neurons pass

115
00:04:42,494 --> 00:04:43,639
through each position.

116
00:04:44,381 --> 00:04:46,639
Use a threshold to pick out the hot spots.

117
00:04:47,381 --> 00:04:49,476
Cluster to decide the subdivisions.

118
00:04:50,219 --> 00:04:52,451
Recruit the local neurons into each one.

119
00:04:53,194 --> 00:04:55,106
Draw the boundary of each candidate from

120
00:04:55,106 --> 00:04:56,651
where those neurons cluster.

121
00:04:57,394 --> 00:04:59,181
Compute a value that describes how the

122
00:04:59,181 --> 00:05:01,101
fibers are spread out inside it.

123
00:05:01,844 --> 00:05:03,869
And last, check whether the region has

124
00:05:03,869 --> 00:05:05,651
long range tracts of its own.

125
00:05:06,394 --> 00:05:08,226
Two places are worth noticing.

126
00:05:08,969 --> 00:05:10,769
The threshold in the second step can be

127
00:05:10,769 --> 00:05:12,719
changed, and if you change it, the

128
00:05:12,719 --> 00:05:15,644
boundaries move. The seventh step is the

129
00:05:15,644 --> 00:05:17,114
one that steps outside.

130
00:05:17,856 --> 00:05:20,006
The first six all move around inside the

131
00:05:20,006 --> 00:05:22,369
same distribution; the seventh brings in

132
00:05:22,369 --> 00:05:24,356
an independent kind of evidence, the

133
00:05:24,356 --> 00:05:26,744
direction the tracts run, to confirm that

134
00:05:26,744 --> 00:05:28,469
what the first six found is not a

135
00:05:28,469 --> 00:05:30,051
statistical artifact.

136
00:05:31,426 --> 00:05:33,151
This is the evidence the seventh step

137
00:05:33,151 --> 00:05:35,451
uses: fifty eight bundles of fiber that

138
00:05:35,451 --> 00:05:38,071
cross between regions along fixed paths.

139
00:05:38,814 --> 00:05:41,571
Fourteen commissures, ten paired chiasms,

140
00:05:41,614 --> 00:05:43,084
twelve paired connectives.

141
00:05:43,826 --> 00:05:46,201
For a candidate unit to stand, at least

142
00:05:46,201 --> 00:05:47,721
one of these has to touch it.

143
00:05:48,464 --> 00:05:50,776
In other words, having a local circuit is

144
00:05:50,776 --> 00:05:53,164
not enough. It also has to

145
00:05:53,164 --> 00:05:54,409
talk to the outside.

146
00:05:55,782 --> 00:05:58,132
The criterion produced one by-product that

147
00:05:58,132 --> 00:06:00,002
is also its strongest defence.

148
00:06:00,744 --> 00:06:03,069
A block called the V L P was split into a

149
00:06:03,069 --> 00:06:05,419
back half and a front half — two separate

150
00:06:05,419 --> 00:06:08,344
units. It is the only case in the whole

151
00:06:08,344 --> 00:06:10,752
brain of two units inside a single block.

152
00:06:11,494 --> 00:06:13,044
Three independent things support the

153
00:06:13,044 --> 00:06:15,969
split. The cell bodies of the two groups

154
00:06:15,969 --> 00:06:17,527
sit in separate places.

155
00:06:18,269 --> 00:06:20,864
Their fibers project to separate targets.

156
00:06:21,607 --> 00:06:23,682
And each has its own characteristic long

157
00:06:23,682 --> 00:06:25,519
range tracts, talking to different

158
00:06:25,519 --> 00:06:28,227
partners. Why does this matter?

159
00:06:28,969 --> 00:06:31,257
Because if this criterion only rearranged

160
00:06:31,257 --> 00:06:33,219
the fifty eight blocks, it would add no

161
00:06:33,219 --> 00:06:36,169
information at all. Instead it cut two

162
00:06:36,169 --> 00:06:38,352
working units out of a block that looks,

163
00:06:38,407 --> 00:06:40,139
to the eye, like one thing.

164
00:06:40,882 --> 00:06:43,164
That is the payoff for changing criteria.

165
00:06:44,546 --> 00:06:48,103
Lesson five. What the criterion produced.

166
00:06:48,846 --> 00:06:50,141
Across the whole brain:

167
00:06:50,183 --> 00:06:53,583
forty one units. Nineteen pairs, plus

168
00:06:53,583 --> 00:06:55,096
three unpaired ones sitting on the

169
00:06:55,096 --> 00:06:58,208
midline. Four further pairs of blocks had

170
00:06:58,208 --> 00:07:00,596
no local neurons of their own — only large

171
00:07:00,596 --> 00:07:02,571
numbers of projecting terminals passing

172
00:07:02,571 --> 00:07:04,766
through, and no local processing.

173
00:07:05,508 --> 00:07:07,266
The paper calls those hubs.

174
00:07:08,008 --> 00:07:09,796
And about two of them it raises a very

175
00:07:09,796 --> 00:07:12,208
honest possibility: they may simply be too

176
00:07:12,208 --> 00:07:14,408
small in volume to fit any extra local

177
00:07:14,408 --> 00:07:17,583
neurons in. If that is right, then "no

178
00:07:17,583 --> 00:07:19,633
local processing" is not a property of

179
00:07:19,633 --> 00:07:21,733
those regions. It is a

180
00:07:21,733 --> 00:07:23,378
consequence of their size.

181
00:07:24,765 --> 00:07:26,735
This is the core figure of the episode.

182
00:07:27,478 --> 00:07:29,353
The table of plus and minus signs in

183
00:07:29,353 --> 00:07:31,603
column A is the most concentrated result

184
00:07:31,603 --> 00:07:34,578
in the paper. It switches the criterion

185
00:07:34,578 --> 00:07:36,578
for classifying a brain region from what

186
00:07:36,578 --> 00:07:38,103
it looks like to whether it has local

187
00:07:38,103 --> 00:07:40,990
neurons of its own. Panel B is where the

188
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:44,340
forty one units sit. Panel C is the four

189
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:47,765
pairs of hubs. Panel D overlays them, and

190
00:07:47,765 --> 00:07:49,848
together they nearly fill the whole brain.

191
00:07:50,590 --> 00:07:52,928
One aside: this figure is also the first

192
00:07:52,928 --> 00:07:54,885
place to go when checking the numbers.

193
00:07:55,628 --> 00:07:57,623
The last lesson comes back to it.

194
00:07:59,009 --> 00:08:02,109
Lesson six. What you can do once you have

195
00:08:02,109 --> 00:08:05,366
units. Counting a connection is direct.

196
00:08:06,109 --> 00:08:08,246
If one projecting neuron has fibers in

197
00:08:08,246 --> 00:08:10,584
region A and region B, that counts as a

198
00:08:10,584 --> 00:08:12,141
connection between the two.

199
00:08:12,884 --> 00:08:15,021
Tally every neuron and you get a matrix of

200
00:08:15,021 --> 00:08:17,229
who connects to whom, and how densely.

201
00:08:17,971 --> 00:08:20,209
Cluster that matrix, and four densely

202
00:08:20,209 --> 00:08:22,016
interconnected families appear.

203
00:08:22,759 --> 00:08:24,204
They match known function:

204
00:08:24,271 --> 00:08:26,641
hearing, vision, movement, smell.

205
00:08:27,384 --> 00:08:28,934
That result is itself a kind of

206
00:08:28,934 --> 00:08:31,759
validation. The team did not tell the

207
00:08:31,759 --> 00:08:33,634
algorithm in advance which regions have

208
00:08:33,634 --> 00:08:35,079
anything to do with hearing.

209
00:08:35,821 --> 00:08:37,709
Those groupings came out of the connection

210
00:08:37,709 --> 00:08:39,909
numbers by themselves, and they agree with

211
00:08:39,909 --> 00:08:42,441
decades of accumulated functional anatomy.

212
00:08:43,812 --> 00:08:45,520
On screen is that matrix.

213
00:08:46,262 --> 00:08:48,237
In panel A you can see that connections

214
00:08:48,237 --> 00:08:50,225
within one half of the brain are visibly

215
00:08:50,225 --> 00:08:51,862
denser than connections crossing the

216
00:08:51,862 --> 00:08:55,025
midline. Brains prefer to process close to

217
00:08:55,025 --> 00:08:58,282
home. Panels C and D are the clustering,

218
00:08:58,362 --> 00:08:59,962
and the four colours are those four

219
00:08:59,962 --> 00:09:02,600
functional families. Here is one

220
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,345
immediately usable example.

221
00:09:05,087 --> 00:09:07,012
A search in the database returns about

222
00:09:07,012 --> 00:09:08,662
four hundred neurons connecting the

223
00:09:08,662 --> 00:09:10,525
auditory region with some twenty eight

224
00:09:10,525 --> 00:09:13,687
other regions. Set aside the dense link

225
00:09:13,687 --> 00:09:15,450
between the left and right auditory

226
00:09:15,450 --> 00:09:17,700
regions, and about a fifth of them connect

227
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:20,570
on both sides to a region called C V L P.

228
00:09:21,312 --> 00:09:23,375
So there is now a hypothesis you can take

229
00:09:23,375 --> 00:09:25,912
into the lab: C V L P may be the next

230
00:09:25,912 --> 00:09:27,625
station for processing auditory

231
00:09:27,625 --> 00:09:30,737
information. A connectivity map does not

232
00:09:30,737 --> 00:09:33,625
hand you the answer. But it turns a needle

233
00:09:33,625 --> 00:09:35,725
in a haystack into "these few needles are

234
00:09:35,725 --> 00:09:37,045
worth testing first".

235
00:09:38,432 --> 00:09:41,577
Lesson seven. Back to that sentence:

236
00:09:41,657 --> 00:09:43,157
this is a definition that can be

237
00:09:43,157 --> 00:09:44,777
overturned by its own data.

238
00:09:45,519 --> 00:09:47,332
Every item that follows is written in the

239
00:09:47,332 --> 00:09:49,469
paper's own discussion and its own list of

240
00:09:49,469 --> 00:09:52,839
limitations. First, the threshold.

241
00:09:53,582 --> 00:09:55,682
The one in the second step, together with

242
00:09:55,682 --> 00:09:58,094
the value computed in the sixth, sets the

243
00:09:58,094 --> 00:10:01,119
boundaries. How sensitive the number forty

244
00:10:01,119 --> 00:10:02,832
one is to that threshold was never

245
00:10:02,832 --> 00:10:05,707
quantified. The authors say themselves

246
00:10:05,707 --> 00:10:07,394
that some units may still be split

247
00:10:07,394 --> 00:10:10,827
further. Second, how many hubs there are.

248
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:13,382
The summary at the front of the paper says

249
00:10:13,382 --> 00:10:17,007
six. The main text lists four pairs, which

250
00:10:17,007 --> 00:10:20,094
would be eight. One paper, not matching

251
00:10:20,094 --> 00:10:23,394
itself. Third, the correspondence between

252
00:10:23,394 --> 00:10:25,294
the forty one units and the fifty eight

253
00:10:25,294 --> 00:10:27,664
anatomical blocks is never tabulated.

254
00:10:28,407 --> 00:10:30,507
Fourth, the step that compressed neurons

255
00:10:30,507 --> 00:10:32,507
into numbers threw away everything inside

256
00:10:32,507 --> 00:10:34,127
a block, irreversibly.

257
00:10:34,869 --> 00:10:36,694
The boundaries are drawn in a space that

258
00:10:36,694 --> 00:10:38,677
has already lost that information.

259
00:10:39,419 --> 00:10:41,702
And fifth, a connection here is inferred,

260
00:10:41,757 --> 00:10:44,719
not observed. Fibers entering the same

261
00:10:44,719 --> 00:10:46,469
region are presumed to have a chance of

262
00:10:46,469 --> 00:10:49,419
touching. Whether a synapse is actually

263
00:10:49,419 --> 00:10:50,594
there, and which way it

264
00:10:50,594 --> 00:10:52,064
points, is unknown.

265
00:10:53,452 --> 00:10:55,627
There is one more loose point, specific to

266
00:10:55,627 --> 00:10:58,589
the hubs. The paper itself says two of

267
00:10:58,589 --> 00:11:00,627
them may just be too small to fit extra

268
00:11:00,627 --> 00:11:03,714
local neurons in. If that is right, the

269
00:11:03,714 --> 00:11:05,664
category "hub" contains two different

270
00:11:05,664 --> 00:11:08,139
things: genuine transfer stations that do

271
00:11:08,139 --> 00:11:10,514
no local processing, and small regions

272
00:11:10,514 --> 00:11:12,384
that would, but cannot fit it in.

273
00:11:13,127 --> 00:11:15,147
The criterion cannot separate them,

274
00:11:15,202 --> 00:11:16,877
because it only asks whether there are

275
00:11:16,877 --> 00:11:18,372
local neurons of its own.

276
00:11:19,114 --> 00:11:20,697
It never asks why not.

277
00:11:22,079 --> 00:11:23,954
None of this says the L P U cannot be

278
00:11:23,954 --> 00:11:26,854
trusted. It says the L P U is an

279
00:11:26,854 --> 00:11:29,279
operational definition, and an operational

280
00:11:29,279 --> 00:11:31,192
definition should come with its operating

281
00:11:31,192 --> 00:11:34,167
conditions. Forty one is not the true

282
00:11:34,167 --> 00:11:35,999
number of regions in a fly brain.

283
00:11:36,742 --> 00:11:38,142
It is the result of running this

284
00:11:38,142 --> 00:11:40,454
criterion, at this threshold, on this

285
00:11:40,454 --> 00:11:43,142
data. Carry that sentence with you when

286
00:11:43,142 --> 00:11:45,117
you cite it, and everything downstream

287
00:11:45,117 --> 00:11:48,079
becomes more honest. The other thing worth

288
00:11:48,079 --> 00:11:50,017
learning is where these limitations came

289
00:11:50,017 --> 00:11:52,924
from. The authors wrote most of them.

290
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:55,904
A paper willing to put "I did not test how

291
00:11:55,904 --> 00:11:58,112
sensitive this number is to my threshold",

292
00:11:58,242 --> 00:12:00,204
and "my summary does not match my main

293
00:12:00,204 --> 00:12:03,217
text", into its own pages, is a paper its

294
00:12:03,217 --> 00:12:05,324
readers can actually use correctly.

295
00:12:06,691 --> 00:12:08,573
Seven lessons about one term.

296
00:12:09,316 --> 00:12:11,261
Here they are as three reflexes.

297
00:12:12,003 --> 00:12:14,941
First. It is a definition, not a

298
00:12:14,941 --> 00:12:18,353
discovery. Forty one is what one criterion

299
00:12:18,353 --> 00:12:19,998
produced from one dataset.

300
00:12:20,741 --> 00:12:23,028
Change the threshold, change the data, and

301
00:12:23,028 --> 00:12:25,773
the number changes. Second.

302
00:12:26,516 --> 00:12:27,748
Know what it measures.

303
00:12:28,491 --> 00:12:29,841
It measures where there is local

304
00:12:29,841 --> 00:12:31,991
processing, using the distribution of

305
00:12:31,991 --> 00:12:34,966
local neurons. It is not measuring which

306
00:12:34,966 --> 00:12:37,066
neurons belong to the same group, and it

307
00:12:37,066 --> 00:12:38,798
is not measuring synapses.

308
00:12:39,541 --> 00:12:42,091
Third. Nearly three quarters of the

309
00:12:42,091 --> 00:12:43,461
neurons are not in it.

310
00:12:44,203 --> 00:12:46,278
The local neurons that define these units

311
00:12:46,278 --> 00:12:48,203
are only about twenty six percent of the

312
00:12:48,203 --> 00:12:51,266
total. Most neurons in the brain project

313
00:12:51,266 --> 00:12:54,053
across regions. They pass through these

314
00:12:54,053 --> 00:12:56,223
boundaries and are not defined by them.

315
00:12:57,590 --> 00:12:59,023
If you remember one thing:

316
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:01,053
how a term gets defined decides what you

317
00:13:01,053 --> 00:13:02,348
can use it to answer.

318
00:13:03,090 --> 00:13:05,203
For any concept you are about to take as a

319
00:13:05,203 --> 00:13:08,085
unit of analysis, ask six things first.

320
00:13:08,828 --> 00:13:11,810
How it is defined. From what data.

321
00:13:12,553 --> 00:13:15,923
By what criterion. What numbers came out.

322
00:13:16,665 --> 00:13:19,215
How it was tested. And where it is

323
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:22,390
currently loose. This episode walked one

324
00:13:22,390 --> 00:13:23,798
term through all six.

325
00:13:24,540 --> 00:13:25,798
See you next time.
